    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5117cbb7-0835-581a-906d-d24bed0276f3",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that the system is already organized so that the variables are in the order ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient.\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-6 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b54526f3-b178-5eef-97d8-b5bc85d5c659",
